ined body) ─┐\nordinary ingest ────────────────────┴─> shared batch ingest\n                                         ├─ verify and persist device op atomically\n                                         ├─ retain body for delivery/recovery\n                                         └─ remove device-op rows when held events expire/drop\n\nstore open ─> one-time recovery from verified committed and held-event bodies\n```\n\nCloses #8160. Covers all four DEVICE_OPS follow-ups: range-sync delivery, transactional ingest, waiting-event cleanup, and one-time upgrade recovery with an explicit incomplete-recovery warning when bodies are unavailable.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- **Before:** range-sync receivers did not populate DEVICE_OPS; held-event expiry could leave rows; legacy stores did not rebuild missing rows.\n- **After:** `FLEET_BUILD_LOCK_BROKER_WAIT=1 ~/tools/fleet-build-lock -- cargo test -p id-events` — 325 passed, 0 failed, 2 ignored. Includes receiver loopback delivery, transaction/batch ingest, expiry/reload cleanup, and recovery for retained committed and held bodies.\n- `rustfmt --check` on changed event-store files and `git diff --check` pass.\n\n## Merge Danger\n\n**Door:** Two-way; the database changes are additive and rollback does not require a data migration.\n\n**Blast Radius:** Narrow — `id-events` event-store ingest, sync, recovery, and expiry handling.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1797507651&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=11265&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F11265&signature=40974aca0fefde068f77fe74e30dd73699a72f3540c00465b0064d9afca39c49\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/11265?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Device-operation data is now retained consistently for accepted, delayed, and synchronized events.\n  * Missing device-operation records can be restored from verified event history when the event store reopens.\n  * Records associated with expired or discarded waiting events are now cleaned up.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","labels":[{"id":13198400136,"node_id":"LA_kwDOJWP4788AAAADEq-aiA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/labels/audit:complete","name":"audit:complete","description":"PR fully implemented spawning issue","color":"0e8a16","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-17T11:40:47Z","updated_at":"2026-11-24T02:24:47Z","closed_at":"2026-11-17T12:11:50Z","merged_at":"2026-11-17T12:11:50Z","merge_commit_sha":"4fdbd896dc28f1692a876548910d6e163765869f","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[{"id":7767549,"node_id":"T_kwDOAZNvF84AdoX9","url":"https://api.github.com/organizations/26439447/team/7767549","members_url":"https://api.github.com/organizations/26439447/team/7767549/members{/member}","name":"codeowners","description":"Team Discussions: developing-today/code","permission":"pull","privacy":"closed","no